// Verlet step
const oldX = this.x;
const oldY = this.y;

// Apply forces
this.vx += this.gravityDir.x * GRAVITY_STRENGTH;
this.vy += this.gravityDir.y * GRAVITY_STRENGTH;

// Apply input
if (keys.left) this.vx -= MOVE_ACCEL;
if (keys.right) this.vx += MOVE_ACCEL;

// Friction
if (!keys.left && !keys.right) {
  this.vx *= FRICTION;
}

// Update position
this.x += this.vx;
this.y += this.vy;

// Collision resolution
// ...

// Convert back to velocity for next frame
this.px = oldX;
this.py = oldY;
this.vx = this.x - this.px;
this.vy = this.y - this.py;
```

This is proper Verlet integration. The velocity is implicit (derived from position difference).

